{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-explainer-about-soccer-and-famous-football-players/audio/main-f353b83cf627.mp3","durationSec":150.888,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":4.04,"text":"Soccer, also called football, is a game between two teams."},{"start":5.02,"end":7.04,"text":"Each team usually has eleven players."},{"start":7.86,"end":9.76,"text":"Players move the ball mainly with their feet."},{"start":10.46,"end":14.98,"text":"They try to put the ball into the other team’s goal, the large net at the end of the field."},{"start":15.7,"end":17.28,"text":"One goal gives one point."},{"start":18,"end":19.46,"text":"The team with more goals wins."},{"start":20.52,"end":23.52,"text":"If both teams have the same score, the result is a draw."},{"start":24.32,"end":27.56,"text":"A normal soccer match has two halves of 45 minutes."},{"start":28.3,"end":31.02,"text":"The referee can add extra minutes when play stops."},{"start":31.98,"end":34.8,"text":"Most players cannot touch the ball with their hands or arms."},{"start":35.64,"end":40.62,"text":"The goalkeeper can use their hands inside the penalty area, the large box near the goal."},{"start":41.42,"end":47.14,"text":"A foul happens when a player breaks a rule, for example by kicking another player instead of the ball."},{"start":48.84,"end":51.22,"text":"Players have different jobs, called positions."},{"start":52.26,"end":53.48,"text":"Goalkeepers protect the goal."},{"start":53.48,"end":55.94,"text":"Defenders try to stop attacks."},{"start":55.94,"end":58.48,"text":"Midfielders connect defense and attack."},{"start":59.1,"end":60.28,"text":"Forwards try to score goals."},{"start":60.64,"end":62.54,"text":"Some players change how a position works."},{"start":63.24,"end":68.78,"text":"German goalkeeper Manuel Neuer often moved far from his goal to pass the ball or stop an attack early."},{"start":69.28,"end":72.08,"text":"People call this active style a sweeper-keeper style."},{"start":72.52,"end":74.1,"text":"Great players need a strong team."},{"start":74.6,"end":78.28,"text":"Players pass the ball, move into open spaces, and help one another."},{"start":79.22,"end":82.34,"text":"Argentina showed this teamwork at the 2022 FIFA World Cup."},{"start":82.86,"end":85.66,"text":"Captain Lionel Messi scored two goals in the final."},{"start":86.24,"end":89.44,"text":"Goalkeeper Emiliano Martínez also made an important late save."},{"start":90.08,"end":94.48,"text":"Argentina and France drew 3–3, and Argentina won the penalty shootout."},{"start":94.92,"end":98.24,"text":"One star was important, but the whole team created the victory."},{"start":99.3,"end":101.46,"text":"Women’s soccer has many famous stars."},{"start":102.12,"end":107.02,"text":"Marta, from Brazil, scored 17 goals in FIFA Women’s World Cup matches, a World Cup record."},{"start":107.46,"end":110.76,"text":"She is known for skillful movement and close control of the ball."},{"start":110.76,"end":116.14,"text":"Homare Sawa captained Japan when the team won the 2011 Women’s World Cup."},{"start":116.7,"end":121.54,"text":"She scored five goals in that tournament and received the Golden Boot as its top scorer."},{"start":122.48,"end":127.82,"text":"A player can become famous through skill, records, trophies, and exciting moments."},{"start":128.8,"end":136.42,"text":"Brazilian star Pelé won the men’s World Cup three times: in 1958, 1962, and 1970."},{"start":137.48,"end":143.14,"text":"Cristiano Ronaldo of Portugal has won five Ballon d’Or awards, which honor an outstanding player."},{"start":143.94,"end":150.42,"text":"These famous football players have different styles, but both scored many goals and inspired fans around the world."}],"words":[{"text":"Soccer","start":0,"end":0.44},{"text":"also","start":0.82,"end":1.12},{"text":"called","start":1.12,"end":1.42},{"text":"football","start":1.42,"end":1.9},{"text":"is","start":2.12,"end":2.54},{"text":"a","start":2.54,"end":2.72},{"